<p dir=3D"auto">Keyframe interval of the video stream. Keyframes are a full=
 frame encoding, whereas intermediate frames are differential representatio=
ns of the changes between frames.  Keyframes are larger and require more co=
mputing power to process. Higher GOP intervals mean fewer keyframes and as =
a  result, less accurate representation of the video.  Lower GOP rates incr=
ease the accuracy of the  video at the expense of higher bandwidth and comp=
ute load. It is necessary to click the Apply button to enact these changes =
on the camera.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Note that some cameras may have an option for Dynamic GOP o=
r Adaptive Framerate, or some other name for a process that reduces the GOP=
 automatically based on the lack of motion in the camera view. It is advise=
d to turn this feature off when using onvif-gui. To access the feature, use=
 the camera web application from the System Tab -&gt; Browser button.</p>
