<p dir=3D"auto">The drop down box can be used to the select the camera prof=
ile that will be recorded to disk. The Record Profile can be different than=
 the Display Profile shown in the application. This setting can be used mos=
t effectively when the application is configured to show the low resolution=
 substream profile in the display, and use the high resolution main profile=
 as the recording source. This enables the application to maintain real tim=
e display status, especially with multiple streams, while preserving high r=
esolution accuracy in the recorded stream. Because the recorded stream in n=
ot decoded, but rather is piped directly from the camera to disk, the high =
resolution recording presents very little compute load on the host.</p>
