<p dir=3D"auto">You will now be starting from a clean slate. The following =
text saved into the <code>smb.conf</code> file will create a sharing config=
uration that is compatible with the application. For this configuration, yo=
u will need to know the account under which Onvif GUI was installated. For =
example, if you created a user onvif-gui, and were logged on as that user d=
uring the time the appliation was installed, the default directory for the =
application will be /home/onvif-gui. The configuration shown below will sha=
re two sub-directories used by the program, namely Videos and Pictures.</p>
<div class=3D"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overf=
low-auto"><pre class=3D"notranslate"><code>[global]
  workgroup =3D WORKGROUP

[Videos]
  comment =3D Shared Videos Folder
  path =3D /home/onvif-gui/Videos
  browasble =3D yes
  read only =3D yes

[Pictures]
  comment =3D Shared Pictures Folder
  path =3D /home/onvif-gui/Pictures
  browsable =3D yes
  read only =3D yes

[Documents]
  comment =3D Shared Documents Folder
  path =3D /home/onvif-gui/Documents
  browsable =3D yes
  read only =3D no
</code></pre><div class=3D"zeroclipboard-container">
    <clipboard-copy aria-label=3D"Copy" class=3D"ClipboardButton btn btn-in=
visible js-clipboard-copy m-2 p-0 d-flex flex-justify-center flex-items-cen=
ter" data-copy-feedback=3D"Copied!" data-tooltip-direction=3D"w" value=3D"[=
global]
  workgroup =3D WORKGROUP

[Videos]
  comment =3D Shared Videos Folder
  path =3D /home/onvif-gui/Videos
  browasble =3D yes
  read only =3D yes

[Pictures]
  comment =3D Shared Pictures Folder
  path =3D /home/onvif-gui/Pictures
  browsable =3D yes
  read only =3D yes

[Documents]
  comment =3D Shared Documents Folder
  path =3D /home/onvif-gui/Documents
