<p dir=3D"auto">A virtual environment Folder is a subdirectory on the disk =
containing all the files necessary to run a particular version of Python. T=
his allows a Python version separate from the system installed version to o=
perate independently. Python has been optimized to minimize the size of the=
 Folder, so the virtual environments are lightwieght. The virtual environme=
nt Folder is created by a call to the venv module as <code>python3 -m venv =
&lt;name&gt;</code>, where <code>&lt;name&gt;</code> is chosen by the user.=
 Note that <code>&lt;name&gt;</code> is traditionally entered as a relative=
 path name, but a full path name is valid. Note that some Linux distributio=
ns have the venv module included by default, while other distributions requ=
ire the installation of additional libraries.</p>
</li>
<li>
<div class=3D"markdown-heading" dir=3D"auto"><h4 tabindex=3D"-1" class=3D"h=
eading-element" dir=3D"auto">Shell Variables</h4><a id=3D"user-content-shel=
