<p dir=3D"auto"><b>Virtiofs needs shared memory to work</b>. This can be en=
abled in the hardware configuration window. Navigate to Hardware -&gt; Memo=
ry and select Enable shared memory, then click the Apply button.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">After that, open virt-manager and select the virtual machin=
e while it is not running. Click the Open Icon, and then click the blue cir=
cle i button. The virt-manager hardware window will be shown. The left pane=
 contains the different categories. The right pane contains the setting for=
 the specific category. Beneath the categorey pane, there is a button calle=
d 'Add Hardware'. A dialog box should pop up. In the pane on the left, clic=
k on Filesystem.</p>
