<details><summary>Application Icon on Linux</summary>
<p dir=3D"auto">&nbsp;</p>
<hr>
<p dir=3D"auto">An icon launcher can improve usability for the application,=
 especially for non-technical users. On Linux, the desktop icons are config=
ured with .desktop files, which can reside either in the users <code>$HOME/=
.local/share/applications</code> folder, or in the system <code>/usr/share/=
applications</code> folder. Launchers placed in the system location will re=
quire sudo access to install.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">A typical .desktop file is shown below. This file was writt=
en for a bare metal install of the program in a python virtual environment.=
